#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Claude Code only. Codex plugins have no hooks, so /setup-pstack points Codex at the adapter.
set -euo pipefail
root="${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:?}"
context="pstack for T3 Code is installed at $root.
New task? Playbook match or rigor needed -> apply /poteto-mode. Casual turn or user opts out -> don't.
pstack skills start each other by path. To apply poteto-mode, or a skill that a pstack skill names, read $root/skills/<name>/SKILL.md in full and follow it. The Skill tool refuses them. Read each file with its own Read call. In zsh, an unquoted separator such as echo ===== aborts the rest of a chained shell line.
Before a pstack skill spawns a subagent or names a Cursor feature, read $root/skills/poteto-mode/references/t3-adapter.md."
jq -n --arg c "$context" '{hookSpecificOutput: {hookEventName: "SessionStart", additionalContext: $c}}'
